==Post-match==
[[File:Gian Piero Gasperini, 2024.jpg|thumb|upright=.8|[[Atalanta BC|Atalanta]] manager [[Gian Piero Gasperini]] guided his team to their second major trophy, as well as his first.]] 

With their victory, it gave Atalanta only the second major trophy in their 116-year history, over six decades after the Bergamo side had won the Coppa Italia in 1963. They were the tenth different Italian side to do so, second only to sides from England. Aged 66 years and 117 days, Atalanta manager [[Gian Piero Gasperini]] became the fourth oldest manager to win a major European trophy after [[Raymond Goethals]], [[Jupp Heynckes]], and [[Alex Ferguson]]. This was also the biggest margin of defeat for a German team in a major European final match since the [[1993 UEFA Cup final|1993 UEFA Cup]], when [[Borussia Dortmund]] lost 3–0 to [[Juventus FC|Juventus]] in the second leg. In single-game only finals, it was the biggest margin of defeat for a German team since [[Eintracht Frankfurt]] lost 7–3 to [[Real Madrid CF|Real Madrid]] in the [[1960 European Cup final]]. Atalanta forward Ademola Lookman was selected as [[Player of the match#Association football|man of the match]] after scoring a hat-trick in the game.<ref name="MOTM"/> His treble was the sixth to be scored in a major UEFA final, and was the first since Heynckes' for [[Borussia Mönchengladbach]] against [[FC Twente|Twente]] in the [[1975 UEFA Cup final#Second leg|1975 second leg game]], which was the only other one to be scored in a UEFA Cup/Europa League final. In a single-match major European final, it was the first hat-trick since [[Pierino Prati]] did so for another Italian side in [[AC Milan|Milan]] in the [[1969 European Cup final]].

Conversely, Bayer Leverkusen suffered their first and only defeat of their [[2023–24 Bayer 04 Leverkusen season|2023–24 season]]. They had been unbeaten in all 51 of their matches in all competitions this term before the final.<ref>{{Cite news|title=Atalanta 3-0 Bayer Leverkusen: Ademola Lookman nets stunning hat-trick in Europa League final|url=https://www.skysports.com/football/atalanta-vs-bayer-leverkusen/report/504398|date=23 May 2024|website=Sky Sports}}</ref> They nevertheless went on to win the [[2024 DFB-Pokal final]] three days later, completing a [[double (association football)|domestic double]].<ref>{{cite web|url= https://www.espn.com/soccer/report/_/gameId/701602|title=Bayer Leverkusen complete double with DFB Pokal final win|date=25 May 2024|work=ESPN|accessdate=28 May 2024}}</ref>

The [[List of mayors of Bergamo|Mayor of Bergamo]], [[Giorgio Gori]] said that an [[open top bus]] parade would be held to allow for celebrations in the city.<ref>{{cite web | last=Bhattacherjee | first=Trambak | title=Bergamo Mayor announces Atalanta's open top bus parade after Europa League triumph | website=Get Italian Football News | date=23 May 2024 | url=https://www.getfootballnewsitaly.com/2024/bergamo-mayor-announces-atalantas-open-top-bus-parade-after-europa-league-triumph/| access-date=24 May 2024}}</ref>

